+.. _custom-visualization-display-name:
+
+Customize node labels with ``display_name``
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+By default, each node is labeled with its Python identifier and type. To show a human-readable label without renaming the function, add a ``display_name`` tag with the ``@tag`` function modifier (learn more :ref:`tag-decorators`):
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    from hamilton.function_modifiers import tag
+
+    @tag(display_name="My Custom Display Name")
+    def node_with_display_name(input_a: int) -> int:
+        return input_a + 1
+
+The label is resolved in this order:
+
+1. An explicitly supplied name parameter (e.g., when calling the graphviz creation logic directly).
+2. The node's ``display_name`` tag value.
+3. The node's Python identifier.
+
+If ``display_name`` holds a list, the first element is used; an empty list falls back to the node name. All resolved display names are HTML-escaped before being embedded in the label, so special characters such as ``<``, ``>``, ``&``, and quotes render correctly.
